    {
      "id": "mM1urbna8ASnus_1xtlrs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 663.8123020337048,
      "y": 2022.2806861270897,
      "width": 636.699462890625,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 89731521,
      "version": 1295,
      "versionNonce": 788182372,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1767002073893,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. we are extracting the username from the github.com\nfirst we initialize input \nlet's say input  = githcom/yogeshk34/\n\n! 1st step we trim the input  to remove any whitespace \nfor ex:  githcom/yogeshk34 /\nso this'll become \n=> githcom/yogeshk34/ (all whitespaces removed)\n\n! 2nd step : remove the protocol (if present)\ninput = https://github.com/yogeshk34/\n\nthen we have to remove the protocol and the slashes after that\nhttps:// & http://\n\ncleaned = trimmed.replace(/^https?:\\/\\/ /,' ');\nso the patttern is as follows : \n1. / / regex starts, all inside this is to be followed\n2. ^ check at the start \n3. ? optional, written after the word you wanna check \n4. \\ replace the symbol afterwards, (replace /)\n5. ' ' taking a guess that all this will be replaced by a whitespace\n\n! 3rd step: remove www (same as protocol)\ncleaned = trimmed.replace(/^www\\./,' ');\n \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. we are extracting the username from the github.com\nfirst we initialize input \nlet's say input  = githcom/yogeshk34/\n\n! 1st step we trim the input  to remove any whitespace \nfor ex:  githcom/yogeshk34 /\nso this'll become \n=> githcom/yogeshk34/ (all whitespaces removed)\n\n! 2nd step : remove the protocol (if present)\ninput = https://github.com/yogeshk34/\n\nthen we have to remove the protocol and the slashes after that\nhttps:// & http://\n\ncleaned = trimmed.replace(/^https?:\\/\\/ /,' ');\nso the patttern is as follows : \n1. / / regex starts, all inside this is to be followed\n2. ^ check at the start \n3. ? optional, written after the word you wanna check \n4. \\ replace the symbol afterwards, (replace /)\n5. ' ' taking a guess that all this will be replaced by a whitespace\n\n! 3rd step: remove www (same as protocol)\ncleaned = trimmed.replace(/^www\\./,' ');\n \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "34K0IVveF3rFDuqgOA3Gd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1457.9673592695863,
      "y": 1999.3038090247114,
      "width": 727.5193481445312,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1278095343,
      "version": 3015,
      "versionNonce": 1530970844,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1767002073893,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "// extract the username \n1. check if the the variable contains github.com\nif(cleaned.includes('github.com/')) {\n    // here also we check for trailing slashes  \n    // for ex: github.com/yogeshk34//\n    cleaned.replace(/\\/+$/,'')\n    \n    // so the above pattern works as follows \n    1. // start and end of regex \n    2. \\/ replace the literal / slash \n    3. + replace multiple occurrences\n    4. & check always at the end \n    // $ is opposite of ^\n\n2. once trailing slashes have been checked\nwe'll probably get a url like \ngithub.com/yogeshk34\n\nnow we want to extracct the username so we'll split \nby /\ncause that'll give us github.com & yogeshk34 we want \n(yogeshk34)\n\nconst parts = cleaned.split('/')\nreturn parts[parts.length-1]  || '';\nsee this is the confusing part so parts var is github.com & yogeshk34\nso when we return it we're returning github.com whereas we should be \nreturning yogeshk34? why this or am I wrong? cause length-1 meaning 2 -1 \n1 & on the 1st position it is github.com or wait it's inside an array\nso it will be at 1 index & at the first index we have yogeshk34\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "// extract the username \n1. check if the the variable contains github.com\nif(cleaned.includes('github.com/')) {\n    // here also we check for trailing slashes  \n    // for ex: github.com/yogeshk34//\n    cleaned.replace(/\\/+$/,'')\n    \n    // so the above pattern works as follows \n    1. // start and end of regex \n    2. \\/ replace the literal / slash \n    3. + replace multiple occurrences\n    4. & check always at the end \n    // $ is opposite of ^\n\n2. once trailing slashes have been checked\nwe'll probably get a url like \ngithub.com/yogeshk34\n\nnow we want to extracct the username so we'll split \nby /\ncause that'll give us github.com & yogeshk34 we want \n(yogeshk34)\n\nconst parts = cleaned.split('/')\nreturn parts[parts.length-1]  || '';\nsee this is the confusing part so parts var is github.com & yogeshk34\nso when we return it we're returning github.com whereas we should be \nreturning yogeshk34? why this or am I wrong? cause length-1 meaning 2 -1 \n1 & on the 1st position it is github.com or wait it's inside an array\nso it will be at 1 index & at the first index we have yogeshk34\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
